   174	## 7. Progression plan
   175	
   176	**Vocabulary** (this series' own): fragment, notice, integration, acquisition (directed), engagement (clinical — non-hostile), Path, declaration, tier, rank, Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver/Gold, Arbiter, sigil, idle state, deployment, the hold, discharge, the reading (surface / deep), mending, reserve, the line, quiet ground → the Quieting, perimeter, radius, stake, the board, HOLD, outcome, the wall. The system's voices are the **log** (Cael's inventory), the **notice** (one only, the tenth), and **Pike's ledger lines**. Interface text appears only where the canon calls for it.
   177	
   178	**Density targets** (≈58 per 10k overall, front-loaded about 1.7x): **first third ≈81 per 10k** (M1 ≈82, M2 ≈82, M3 ≈78); **middle third ≈48** (M4 ≈50, with the line's mechanics taught as trials; M5 ≈42, with the acquisition spike; M6 ≈40); **final third ≈46** (M7 ≈40, M8 ≈55 with the inventory and the map). After M4 the system surfaces only at genuine turns: the notice, the self-readings, the rim, the fixed point, the inventory.
   179	
   180	**How the first third teaches hard without spending anything:** the log's inventory of nine, with each fragment's idle rent named (Shadow at dusk, Anchor wanting doorways, Storm heavy); the discipline of holding as a skill with failure modes; the board's arithmetic (outcome, not tier); the carters' "don't declare"; the ford's discharge finding; the shale-backs' flight; Oryn's Tide taught in full (contact only, the reserve, three mendings a day, cannot heal herself, "cannot mend what I can't read," two readings); tier talk at the plank (Pike's Copper Force, Teague's unreported Bronze, Lira's Iron R1, Brom's Copper forever). **Cael deploys nothing in M1–M3 except the single ford burst.** The log reads "Deployment since the Line: one" from day 53 to day 90, and the edition keeps that count.
   181	
