    62	
    63	Day 84: a hundred and sixteen in hand, six owed to the smith for a cart in a gorge. Three ribs taped, a calf bound in her cloth, a leg that is new, an ankle taped, a wrist mended and not to pull. Three failed readings, and a healer who wants a fourth "when you're not broken." Thornwater in nine days. Two people out here are measuring him, and neither has a seal.
