   215	---
   216	
   217	Brom's arm took less. He sat with the forearm across his knee and the cloth off it, the wrist open in a mouth two fingers long, and she put her hands either side of the open place, and went still for the seconds, and said "Iron Skin," and Brom said "Yes," and she said "Then it should have closed in a month and hasn't, because you've pulled on it. Dogs?" and Brom said "Dog," and she asked nothing else. It took the time it takes to eat an apple. The mouth at the wrist closed under her hands as the leg had, and when she took them off, the arm from wrist to elbow was a raised dark line and nothing else, and Brom looked at it with the lock face and then, for once, without it.
   218	
   219	"Don't pull on it for a week," she said. "It's not a dog's business now. It's yours."
   220	
   221	She had gone greyer, and sat again, not long, and Cael counted that she had drunk half the skin.
   222	
   223	Karis was awake, against the box. She had watched the leg and the arm with the look she gave a primary source, and said, when Oryn came to her, before Oryn had knelt: "There's nothing wrong with me."
