    24	
    25	"Seventy," said Brom. He had come up behind them without a sound, as a large man can who has spent sixteen days with nothing in his hands. "That's more than the six lines we've got. All of them put together."
    26	
    27	"By eight," said Karis.
    28	
    29	"What's a high traverse?" said Lira. "In a carter's mouth. I know what it is on a hill."
