    40	
    41	Karis had her notebook out, and her pencil was already turning in her fingers.
    42	
    43	"What does he call a map?" she said. "I've a registry sheet in the middle box with the whole continent on it, printed, and a calfskin that a carter drew for his own wheels. They aren't the same kind of thing. Which does he want?"
    44	
    45	"He wants to know where a wheel goes and where it doesn't. He's a ford-keeper. He'll have no more letters than he needs to count a toll." Pike thought about it. "Draw it so a man can follow it with his finger. Put the numbers where he can find them if he's a mind to."
    46	
