    60	
    61	The second was that nobody's finger was on it. The last large slip they took had carried a captain's name in capitals. A one-armed man had struck that name with his own pen before a meadow, and they had gone down to a river under the weight of it. This one had been posted for anyone at all. If they took it they would take it off nobody, and the first line on the sheet could read it when he came down and find nothing in it that was his.
    62	
