   182	
   183	"And you write it," she said. "One line. I'll give you the figures in the order of the columns, and I shan't give them twice unless you ask."
   184	
   185	Lira went, with her Path where she had kept it since the ford. She ran lightly, well in from the edge, and her right foot came down a shade behind her left, and he looked at the gorge until she was a small figure standing a stone on end. She walked back.
   186	
   187	"Slab," she said. "Good slab, all the way. Dry. It rings a bit hollow about halfway, on the outside, so I kept in."
   188	
   189	He paced it, and his hundredth stride fell eleven yards short of her stone.
   190	
   191	"Mine are bigger," said Lira, with satisfaction.
   192	
