   233	They ate cold. Nobody lit the fire, and nobody proposed it; it lay there in its ring with the rule over it. Brom let the tail-board down by its chains as gently as he could, and one link slipped and struck the frame, a small clear note, like a spoon on a cup.
   234	
   235	It came back off the far wall when he had already begun to apologise for it.
   236	
   237	They listened to it go. Up on the dark slope above them nothing whatever happened.
   238	
   239	"Well," said Brom, very low. "That's one thing it doesn't mind."
   240	
