   244	
   245	*Seventy-third day. The bench, at the end of the eighth hundred. The cart came up the fan this morning in six stages, on a rope over a log, by Brom's reckoning and nobody's Path. Eight lines in Karis's table, all of them mine to write. Lira says that I am paid by the line. Each of the eight says yes.*
   246	
   247	*Above us there is a mountain of plates, and by Pike's rule we are not to be loud under whatever lives on it. We have seen nothing yet but one piece of horn.*
   248	
