   133	It passed between the ninth animal and the tenth. It struck their own shelf between them with a sound like a mallet on a cask, and burst, and the larger half of it leaped out again and went on down the slope toward the bench, so that he felt the blow come up through the slab under him. The piece crossed the lower shelf two hundred yards west of where they sat, taking a spray of plates with it, and dropped into the gorge. A good while afterward the far wall gave the whole of it back, the crack and the knocking and the burst.
