   249	She saw no crack. She would say so afterward to anyone who asked, and nobody ever did.
   250	
   251	At eighty the wall on her left hand moved away from her.
   252	
   253	That was how it seemed. She had been running a hand's breadth from it, and between one stride and the next there was a gap there the width of her arm, with daylight in it. The shelf under her had come off the mountain in one piece and was leaning out.
